{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "b1f0c0de-0001-4a00-9a00-platinumcoin04",
    "name": "PlatinumCoin Pix — Local",
    "description": "Living collection for testing the platform locally, **organized one folder per service**.\n\nIt grows incrementally: every step that adds a public endpoint adds the request here, under its service's folder (convention in CLAUDE.md). Step 48 only finalizes it (pre-request auth, idempotency automation, richer examples).\n\n## How to use\n1. Import this file and `pix-platform.local.postman_environment.json` into Postman; select the **PlatinumCoin Pix — Local** environment.\n2. Run **auth-service → Login (alice)** first — it saves `accessToken` into the environment, so every authenticated request below reuses it automatically.\n3. Base URLs come from `*BaseUrl` env vars (ports mirror `docs/local-dev.md`).\n\nCLI alternative: `newman run tools/postman/pix-platform.postman_collection.json -e tools/postman/pix-platform.local.postman_environment.json`.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "auth-service",
      "description": "Identity service — port 8081. Login issues the HS256 JWT that every other service validates. See services/auth-service/README.md.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Login (alice)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('accessToken present', () => pm.expect(body.accessToken).to.be.a('string'));",
                  "pm.test('tokenType is Bearer', () => pm.expect(body.tokenType).to.eql('Bearer'));",
                  "// Save the token so every authenticated request in this collection reuses it.",
                  "pm.environment.set('accessToken', body.accessToken);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"username\": \"alice\",\n  \"password\": \"alice\"\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{authBaseUrl}}/v1/auth/login",
              "host": ["{{authBaseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["v1", "auth", "login"]
            },
            "description": "Authenticate the seeded user alice (acc-001). On success, saves `accessToken` to the environment."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Login (bob)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.environment.set('accessToken', pm.response.json().accessToken);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"username\": \"bob\",\n  \"password\": \"bob\"\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{authBaseUrl}}/v1/auth/login",
              "host": ["{{authBaseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["v1", "auth", "login"]
            },
            "description": "Authenticate the seeded user bob (acc-002). Switches `accessToken` to bob's token."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Login — bad credentials (401)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('401 Unauthorized', () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));",
                  "pm.test('problem+json with INVALID_CREDENTIALS', () => {",
                  "  const p = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(p.code).to.eql('INVALID_CREDENTIALS');",
                  "  pm.expect(p.correlationId).to.be.a('string');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"username\": \"alice\",\n  \"password\": \"wrong\"\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{authBaseUrl}}/v1/auth/login",
              "host": ["{{authBaseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["v1", "auth", "login"]
            },
            "description": "Wrong password ⇒ 401 application/problem+json (no stack trace). Demonstrates the RFC 7807 error contract."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Me (echo principal)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('userId present', () => pm.expect(body.userId).to.be.a('string'));",
                  "pm.test('accountId present', () => pm.expect(body.accountId).to.be.a('string'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{accessToken}}" }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{authBaseUrl}}/v1/auth/me",
              "host": ["{{authBaseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["v1", "auth", "me"]
            },
            "description": "Return the caller identity the common-lib JwtAuthFilter derived from the bearer token (`{userId, accountId}`). Run a Login request first so `{{accessToken}}` is set. Without the header it returns 401 problem+json (`code: UNAUTHORIZED`)."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Health",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{authBaseUrl}}/actuator/health",
              "host": ["{{authBaseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["actuator", "health"]
            },
            "description": "Actuator health — the contract compose healthchecks rely on. Expect {\"status\":\"UP\"}."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "account-service",
      "description": "Accounts & Pix keys — port 8082. First service backed by DynamoDB. Reads pix_accounts. Run auth-service → Login first so `{{accessToken}}` is set. See services/account-service/README.md.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "My account (from JWT)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('accountId present', () => pm.expect(body.accountId).to.be.a('string'));",
                  "pm.test('status present', () => pm.expect(body.status).to.be.a('string'));",
                  "// Money at the public edge is a decimal BRL string (e.g. \"5000.00\"), never a float.",
                  "pm.test('dailyLimit is a decimal string', () => pm.expect(body.dailyLimit).to.match(/^\\d+\\.\\d{2}$/));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{accessToken}}" }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{accountBaseUrl}}/v1/accounts/me",
              "host": ["{{accountBaseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["v1", "accounts", "me"]
            },
            "description": "The caller's own account (`{accountId, status, dailyLimit}`), derived only from the JWT `accountId` claim — no way to name another account. Login as alice vs bob to see the account track the token. Without the header ⇒ 401 problem+json (`code: UNAUTHORIZED`)."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Internal account lookup",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('accountId echoes the path', () => pm.expect(body.accountId).to.eql('acc-001'));",
                  "// Service-to-service view keeps money as integer cents (a JSON number), not a string.",
                  "pm.test('dailyLimitCents is an integer', () => pm.expect(Number.isInteger(body.dailyLimitCents)).to.be.true);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{accessToken}}" }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{accountBaseUrl}}/internal/accounts/acc-001",
              "host": ["{{accountBaseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["internal", "accounts", "acc-001"]
            },
            "description": "Service-to-service lookup by account id (ADR-0006). Returns integer `dailyLimitCents` for callers that do integer math on the limit. Requires a valid token but is not account-scoped (a purely internal seam). Unknown id ⇒ 404 problem+json (`code: ACCOUNT_NOT_FOUND`)."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Register Pix key (EMAIL)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('keyType echoes the request', () => pm.expect(body.keyType).to.eql('EMAIL'));",
                  "pm.test('keyValue present', () => pm.expect(body.keyValue).to.be.a('string'));",
                  "// Re-running against the same value now returns 409 KEY_ALREADY_EXISTS (global uniqueness)."
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{accessToken}}" },
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"keyType\": \"EMAIL\",\n  \"keyValue\": \"alice@platinum.com\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{accountBaseUrl}}/v1/pix-keys",
              "host": ["{{accountBaseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["v1", "pix-keys"]
            },
            "description": "Register a Pix key. Global uniqueness is enforced by a conditional `PutItem` (`attribute_not_exists(pk)`) — a value already taken by any account ⇒ 409 problem+json (`code: KEY_ALREADY_EXISTS`). EMAIL is normalized (trim + lowercase); a malformed value ⇒ 422 (`code: INVALID_PIX_KEY`). For `keyType: EVP` the server mints a UUID and ignores `keyValue`. Owner comes from the JWT, never the body."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "List my Pix keys",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('body is an array', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json()).to.be.an('array'));",
                  "// The list is scoped to the caller's JWT account — never another account's keys."
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{accessToken}}" }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{accountBaseUrl}}/v1/pix-keys",
              "host": ["{{accountBaseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["v1", "pix-keys"]
            },
            "description": "List the caller's Pix keys (GSI1 query on `ACCOUNT#<accountId from JWT>`). Returns only this account's keys."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Delete a Pix key",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('204 No Content', () => pm.response.to.have.status(204));",
                  "// Deleting another account's key ⇒ 403 KEY_FORBIDDEN (existence revealed on purpose);",
                  "// an absent key ⇒ 404 KEY_NOT_FOUND."
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{accessToken}}" }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{accountBaseUrl}}/v1/pix-keys/alice@platinum.com",
              "host": ["{{accountBaseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["v1", "pix-keys", "alice@platinum.com"]
            },
            "description": "Delete an owned Pix key ⇒ 204. Ownership-guarded: another account's key ⇒ 403 problem+json (`code: KEY_FORBIDDEN`, existence revealed since Pix keys are globally resolvable); an absent key ⇒ 404 (`code: KEY_NOT_FOUND`)."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Health",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{accountBaseUrl}}/actuator/health",
              "host": ["{{accountBaseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["actuator", "health"]
            },
            "description": "Actuator health — the contract compose healthchecks rely on. Expect {\"status\":\"UP\"}."
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
